{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nThe sibling emitter writes candidate fixture specs asserting a criterion should fire or stay silent\nfor a real plan. Those assertions come from history, not current code, so a candidate that\ndisagrees with today's criterion is unseparably either wrong or evidence the criterion drifted.\nAdmitting an unverified candidate is worse than none: a wrong must-fire case encodes a false\npositive as required behavior. One run cannot settle it — 208 of 551 store pairs over byte-identical\nmaterial flipped verdict, so shipped specs use `epochs: 3`/`gate: at_least(2)`.\n\n## Approach\n\n**Run.** The emitter writes one strict-valid candidate spec per criterion, each a `dataset` whose\ncases carry an `expect` of `finding` or `pass`. For each case the runner executes the criterion's\nreal Pass-1 finder via `eval_solver.run_case(prompt_id, case, runner=live, repo_root=repo_root)`\n(`eval_solver.py:322`; kw-only `runner`/`repo_root`) — not `calibrate_criterion`, which only scores\na persisted dataset (`load_eval_spec`, `eval.py:69-78`); this run targets criteria with no spec.\nEach case runs three times; `_fired(verdict)` (a finding present) is the observed verdict; a case\nmatching its `expect` in ≥2 of 3 runs REPRODUCES.\n\n**Disposition.** A reproducing case is kept; a non-reproducing one is withheld to a drift report at\n`docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/fixtures/drift-report.md` (criterion, case id, predicted vs\nobserved behavior, and the provenance id the emitter embeds in the case input — `norm_id` for\nmust-fire, `review_event_uuid` for must-not-fire). To\nwrite a criterion's spec the runner carries the candidate's strict-only fields — `prompt`, `model`,\n`epochs`, `gate`, `coverage_threshold`, `scorers` (the deterministic gating scorer) — UNCHANGED,\nrebuilding `dataset` and `gold_set` (the emitter's 1:1 input/label projection) from only the\nreproducing cases. The spec is written to\n`.rebar/evals/<prompt-id>.eval.yaml` via a temp file + atomic `os.replace` only when the filtered\ndataset is balanced (both-sides-non-empty) with a non-empty\n`gold_set` and `validate_eval_spec(spec, strict=True)` returns zero errors — strict needs that\nnon-empty gold_set and the ≥1 gating scorer these carried fields supply; else the criterion is\nwithheld. The spec carries no posture/tier field (posture is routing, not eval-spec schema). The\nrunner also returns an in-memory summary — admitted/withheld ids, drift entries, total spend —\nasserted by tests; the drift report and admitted specs are the only file outputs (no separate\nadmission-summary file).\n\n**No-shadowing guard.** A user `.rebar/evals/<id>.eval.yaml` WINS over a packaged built-in at load\n(`eval_spec_path` before `_packaged_eval_spec`), so a colliding mined spec would shadow a built-in. The runner therefore SKIPS any criterion whose `<prompt-id>.eval.yaml` is a\npackaged built-in in `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/`. A same-id `.rebar/evals/` file is NOT a shadow —\nit is a prior admission artifact, idempotently overwritten by the atomic write — never skipped.\n\n**Budget enforcement.** Before each criterion the run pre-flights\n`ledger.reserve(estimate_usd, ledger_path=<epic ledger>, cap_usd=250.0, reserve_usd=0.0)` against\nthis epic's `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/fixtures/ledger.jsonl` (reserve_usd=0 ⇒ ceiling\nexactly $250), then `finalize()`s priced ACTUAL usage. Because `finalize` prices real tokens that\ncan exceed the estimate, after EACH `finalize` the run re-reads cumulative actual spend and, if it\nnow meets/exceeds `cap_usd`, halts FATALLY before any further criterion — so $250 bounds actual\nfinalized spend, not just estimates. The estimate key comes from the criterion's `exec` tier in\n`criteria.effective_routing('.', gate_key='plan_review')`: `AGENT`→`criteria-eval-agent`,\n`1-TURN`/`2-STEP`→`criteria-eval-cheap` (`exec: DET` out of scope, stripped before `pass1_chunk` per\nADR 0033). Model parity pinned to production Pass-1 per ADR 0109.\n\n**Failure disposition.** Per criterion the two writes are STRICTLY ORDERED — atomic spec\n`os.replace` FIRST, ledger `finalize()` SECOND — with the ledger the sole resume oracle: a\ncriterion is done iff its stable `run_id = f\"admission-{prompt_id}\"` is in the ledger. This is\ncrash-consistent: crash after the spec write but before `finalize` ⇒ no ledger row ⇒ resume\nre-derives and the atomic write overwrites the orphan spec (one row, one charge); crash after\n`finalize` ⇒ the spec is already on disk. A finalized criterion always has its spec. A transient\nmodel/transport error is RETRYABLE (3 attempts, backoff), then the criterion is left uncompleted (no\nledger row; run continues). Both a `reserve` `BudgetExceeded` and the\npost-`finalize` cap breach are FATAL, stopping the run with all finalized criteria admitted;\n`reconcile` recharges no already-recorded `run_id`.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe admission runner, its disposition logic, the drift-report writer, and the `.rebar/evals/` specs.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Repairing drift (each entry becomes a ticket linked `discovered_from` the epic); editing\n  `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/`; scheduling re-runs (the sibling self-healing loop owns it).\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit tests drive disposition via a stubbed scripted solver (deterministic, no model); the live run\ncovers the real path end to end.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A must-fire case scripted (fire, fire, silent) is admitted into its criterion's written\n      dataset (`pytest`).\n- [ ] A must-fire case scripted (fire, silent, silent) is withheld and writes a drift-report entry\n      naming criterion, case id, predicted/observed behavior, and the embedded provenance id\n      (`norm_id`/`review_event_uuid`) (`pytest`).\n- [ ] With the ledger already at the ceiling, the first criterion's `reserve` raises `BudgetExceeded`\n      and a call-counting stub reports `0` model calls (`pytest`).\n- [ ] When a criterion's finalized ACTUAL spend pushes cumulative spend to/past `cap_usd`, the run\n      halts before the next criterion (breaching one stays admitted); `pytest` uses synthetic\n      rows priced above the estimate and a stub reporting no next calls.\n- [ ] Every written spec returns zero errors from `validate_eval_spec(spec, strict=True)` (the real\n      validator, run by `pytest` over each file).\n- [ ] A criterion matching a packaged built-in in `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/` is skipped, while a\n      same-id `.rebar/evals/` file (a prior artifact) is NOT; `pytest` asserts written and packaged\n      basenames intersect emptily and the pre-seeded `.rebar/evals/` id was still processed.\n- [ ] A criterion whose reproducing cases leave one side empty writes no spec, drifting its cases\n      (`pytest`).\n- [ ] A criterion whose cases raise before all finish writes no partial `.eval.yaml` (`pytest`,\n      mid-criterion failure).\n- [ ] Resume is crash-consistent (`pytest`): a re-run recharges no finalized criterion (`reconcile`\n      returns the existing row for a completed `run_id`, zero new calls); a criterion with a spec\n      file but no ledger row (crash between writes) is re-derived to one ledger row.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] A live admission run has completed over the full candidate set with the Pass-1\n      model pinned to its production class, and this epic's ledger records total spend >0 and ≤250.0\n      with a per-pass model id on every row.\n      provenance: environment=developer workstation against the production Bedrock chain;\n      principal=the Bedrock plan-review identity; privilege_posture=production-equivalent;\n      instrument=live-call.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] Each drift-report entry has a ticket linked `discovered_from` the parent epic.\n      provenance: environment=the rebar tickets store; principal=the session's rebar assignee;\n      privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n`make lint`/`make typecheck`/`make test` pass; live run completed; drift report and admitted specs\ncommitted; cumulative actual ledger spend ≤ $250 (reserve_usd=0, post-finalize halt).\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788422769141772001,"uuid":"c8b158b5-79dc-4543-80b3-54e31a0a8bb8"}